<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistan cotton output reaches 3.31 mln bales.</title>
<headline>Pakistan cotton output reaches 3.31 mln bales.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1996-11-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's cotton output had reached 3.31 million 375-lb bales in the 1996/97 (July/June) crop year by November 1, over 60 percent up on the 2.04 million bales harvested in the year-ago period, ginners said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The private Pakistan Cotton Ginners Association said spinning mills had bought 2.237 million bales, against 1.416 million by the same date last year. Exporters had bought 1,100 bales compared to 51,880 last year, it said.</p>
<p>The association said ginners held 366,852 unsold bales as well as 706,181 unginned press bales as of November 1. --Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
</text>
